## 9. Acceptance criteria

- [ ] `BranchTO` includes `latitude`/`longitude`; `GET /api/branch/fetch_branches` response contains both fields (nullable) — verified by the new backend test.
- [ ] `./mvnw clean verify` from `backend/` passes with counts reported before/after, matching or exceeding the stated baseline (0 new failures).
- [ ] `IBranch` includes `latitude: number | null` and `longitude: number | null`; `npx tsc --noEmit` is clean.
- [ ] `readChosenBranch()`/`writeChosenBranch()`/`clearChosenBranch()` round-trip correctly and never throw on malformed JSON (test asserts this explicitly, mirroring `kioskBranch.test.ts`).
- [ ] `haversineDistanceKm` returns a correct, deterministic km value for at least one known pair of coordinates (test with a fixed expected value).
- [ ] `BranchPickerDrawer` renders and is selectable with `REACT_APP_GOOGLE_MAPS_KEY` unset (no map mounted) — test asserts a branch can be chosen via `onSelect`.
- [ ] A test asserts `navigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition` is NOT called until the "use nearest branch" control is clicked, and IS called exactly once after the click.
- [ ] A branch fixture with `latitude: null, longitude: null` renders in the list, is selectable, and shows no distance value once an origin is resolved — test asserts this explicitly.
- [ ] An ordinary customer (`isKiosk=false`, `isAdmin=false`, `isEditMode=false`) with no stored chosen branch sees `BranchPickerDrawer` mounted with `dismissable=false`; the menu content behind it exists in the DOM but the picker is present.
- [ ] The same customer with a stored chosen branch does NOT see the picker mounted on load.
- [ ] `isKiosk=true` still resolves via `resolveKioskBranchId()`; a kiosk-mode render exercises `KioskBranchSelector`, not `BranchPickerDrawer`, for its own gate.
- [ ] `isAdmin=true` with `branchId` present in the URL resolves to that `adminBranchId`, gate never opens.
- [ ] `isEditMode=true` never opens the customer gate, and `useMenuData`'s `resolveBranchId()` returns the edited order's `branch_id`, not `DEFAULT_BRANCH_ID` or the stored chosen branch.
- [ ] `useCheckout.ts`'s order-creation path uses the chosen branch id (not `DEFAULT_BRANCH_ID`) when one is stored — test asserts `createOrder` is called with it.
- [ ] `BranchScheduleHeader` renders the stored chosen branch's name when one is set, and still falls back to the branch matching `DEFAULT_BRANCH_ID` when none is stored (both cases covered by tests).
- [ ] `HomePageModals.tsx:109`'s delivery precedence line (`availability.branchId ?? pending.branchId`) is unchanged by every sub-task — a diff/test confirms it.
- [ ] The branch chip renders near the hero (non-kiosk, non-admin) labelled with the current branch name, and tapping it reopens the picker — test asserts both.
- [ ] Switching branch with a non-empty cart opens `BranchSwitchWarningDrawer` naming the lines that will be dropped, and confirming removes only those lines from `cartItems` (test asserts the surviving cart contents).
- [ ] Cancelling the switch warning leaves `cartItems` and the stored chosen branch unchanged.
- [ ] `npx tsc --noEmit` clean and `npx jest` green across the whole suite; actual pass/fail counts reported before and after, with the one documented pre-existing `ActiveOrderIslandPill` failure neither newly introduced nor used to mask a regression.
- [ ] No new dependency beyond `@react-google-maps/api`; `stylis` remains pinned at `4.2.0` in `package.json` and `package-lock.json`.
- [ ] No `.env`/`.env.local` file and no literal API key is present in any file written by this task.

## 10. Out of scope

- Any file under `ic-pizza-mobile/`, `ic-pizza-kiosk/`, `ic-pizza-courier/`.
- Any backend file other than `BranchTO.java`, `BranchService.java`, and the one new/extended backend test file (no entity change, no repository change, no other controller/service).
- `src/domains/kiosk/utils/kioskBranch.ts` and `src/domains/kiosk/components/KioskBranchSelector.tsx` — read for convention only, never modified.
- `HomePageModals.tsx:109`'s delivery-precedence expression itself.
- Any Google Distance Matrix / paid distance API call.
- Any dependency other than `@react-google-maps/api`.
- Any `git` command of any kind (add/commit/branch/etc.) — writing the file to disk is the entire "commit" step in this pipeline.
- Reconciling a stored chosen-branch id against a live branch list if the branch was later deactivated (edge case 7, §7) — explicitly not requested by the owner's five answers.
- Any change to how `recommended`/`gift` query params are consumed in `useMenuData.ts` beyond leaving their existing handling untouched.
- Seeding real coordinates for any branch (ST1 only exposes the column; nullability is the point).

## 11. Test plan

Follow `ic-client/.claude/CLAUDE.md` conventions throughout: no `@types/jest`; `jest`/`describe`/`it`/`expect` imported from `@jest/globals`; factoryless `jest.mock()` resolving to `__mocks__/`; `jest.fn<ReturnType, ArgsTuple>()` typed explicitly, never `jest.Mock<...>` as an annotation. Backend tests follow `backend/.claude/CLAUDE.md` (read and follow directly — this file could not be reproduced here due to a read-permission gate encountered while writing this spec; the implementer has full access and must comply with it).

**ST1 (backend):**
- New/extended test in `backend/src/test/java/com/icpizza/backend/domain/branch/`: `GET /api/branch/fetch_branches` response includes non-null `latitude`/`longitude` keys (present, whether or not populated) for at least one branch. Covers brief requirement "backend: `/branch/fetch_branches` returns latitude/longitude".

**ST2:**
- `customerBranch.test.ts`: read/write/clear round-trip; malformed JSON → `null`, never throws; empty string → `null` (mirror `kioskBranch.test.ts` cases exactly).
- `haversine.test.ts`: known coordinate pair → known km value (fixed expected number, e.g. two Bahrain points a few km apart); distance to self is `0`.
- `useBranchResolution.test.ts`: returns stored branch + its id when set; falls back to `{chosenBranch: null, chosenBranchId: DEFAULT_BRANCH_ID}` when unset.
- `public.test.ts`: `fetchPublicBranches` hits `/branch/fetch_branches` with a raw (non-`authFetch`) request and returns the parsed array; propagates a non-ok response as a thrown error, mirroring `fetchBaseAppInfo`'s existing test shape.

**ST3:**
- `BranchListView.test.tsx`: renders every branch by name; a branch with `distances[id] === null` renders with no distance text; `onUseNearestBranch` fires on button click; `locating`/`locationError` render the expected states.
- `BranchMapView.test.tsx`: with the third-party library `jest.doMock`'d, asserts a marker is rendered per branch WITH coordinates and none for a null-coordinate branch; marker click calls `onSelectBranch`.
- `BranchPickerDrawer.test.tsx`: **covers "geolocation is requested ONLY when 'nearest' is pressed, never on mount — assert this explicitly"** — spy/mock `navigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition`, render the drawer, assert zero calls, click the nearest control, assert exactly one call. **Covers "with NO key the picker still renders and a branch can still be chosen"** — render with `GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY` undefined (default test env), assert `BranchMapView` is not rendered and `onSelect` fires from a list-row tap. **Covers "a branch with NULL coordinates is still listed and selectable, with no distance shown"** — fixture branch with `latitude: null, longitude: null`, present in the rendered list, tappable, `onSelect` receives it; after resolving a nearest-branch origin, its row shows no distance while sibling rows do.
- `dismissable=false` renders no close affordance and the Drawer's `onClose` callback is never invoked from a backdrop/Esc simulation.

**ST4:**
- `useMenuData.test.ts`: **"entry is blocked until a branch is chosen, for an ordinary customer"** — no stored branch, `isKiosk=false`, `isAdmin=false`, `isEditMode=false` → `customerBranchGateOpen` becomes `true`. **"the stored choice is reused on the next visit and does NOT block"** — seed `writeChosenBranch` before render → `customerBranchGateOpen` stays `false`, and `fetchBaseAppInfo`/`fetchPublicBranches` is called with the stored branch's id. **"kiosk path unaffected"** — `isKiosk=true` → `resolveBranchId` still calls through to the kiosk resolver, `customerBranchGateOpen` never set from the customer arm. **"admin path unaffected"** — `isAdmin=true` + `adminBranchId` set → that id wins, gate never opens. **Edit-mode case**: `isEditMode=true` with a seeded `orderToEdit.branch_id` → `resolveBranchId()` returns that id, not `DEFAULT_BRANCH_ID`, and the gate never opens.
- `HomePage.test.tsx`: full-stack render (mirroring the existing `renderHomePage` helper) verifying the picker is present when unseeded and absent when a branch is pre-seeded; existing pre-seeded-by-default suite continues to pass unmodified (aside from the added `beforeEach` seeding).
- `HomePageModals.test.tsx`: `BranchPickerDrawer` probe receives `dismissable={false}` and no `onClose` while `customerBranchGateOpen`; its `onSelect` triggers `writeChosenBranch` + `setCustomerBranchGateOpen(false)` + `refreshMenu` in that order (assert via the mocked `refreshMenu`/storage state).

**ST5:**
- `useCheckout.test.ts`: **"the order is created against the CHOSEN branch, not DEFAULT_BRANCH_ID"** — seed a chosen branch different from `DEFAULT_BRANCH_ID`, drive the logged-in-with-name checkout path, assert `createOrder` received that branch id.
- `ClientInfoPopup.test.tsx`: `onSave`'s third argument is the chosen branch id (not `DEFAULT_BRANCH_ID`) when no in-popup branch is selected.
- `BranchScheduleHeader.test.tsx`: new case — a chosen branch other than `DEFAULT_BRANCH_ID` is seeded, its name (not the `DEFAULT_BRANCH_ID`-matched branch's name) renders; existing "falls back to 'IC Pizza'"/`DEFAULT_BRANCH_ID`-matching cases keep passing with the added `localStorage.clear()` `beforeEach`.
- **"delivery precedence: `availability.branchId` still wins over the picked branch"** — a `HomePageModals.test.tsx` case (already exercised in that suite's delivery coverage) re-asserted unchanged: seed a chosen branch different from `AVAILABLE.branchId`, drive `handleDeliveryConfirm`, assert `payForDelivery` receives `AVAILABLE.branchId`, not the chosen branch.

**ST6:**
- `BranchChip.test.tsx`: renders the given `branchName`; `onClick` fires on tap.
- `useBranchSwitch.test.ts`: empty cart → immediate switch, no warning; non-empty cart → warning opens with `warningLoading=true`, then populated `warningUnavailableNames` once `fetchBaseAppInfo` resolves; `confirmSwitch` drops only the named lines from `cartItems` and calls `refreshMenu`; `cancelSwitch` leaves `cartItems` and the stored branch untouched; selecting the already-chosen branch is a no-op; fetch failure surfaces `warningError` and blocks the switch.
- `BranchSwitchWarningDrawer.test.tsx`: shows a spinner while `loading`; lists `unavailableItemNames`; `onConfirm`/`onCancel` fire on their respective buttons; `anchor="bottom"` MUI `Drawer` structure present (rounded corners, drag handle, per convention).
- `HomePage.test.tsx`: integration case — tap the chip, select a different branch with a non-empty cart containing one item unavailable at the target, confirm the warning, assert the cart retains only the available line and the stored branch changed.
- `HeroSection.test.tsx`: chip renders with the resolved branch name from the `branches` prop + stored id; absent when `isKiosk`.
